# Internal tooling stays in the repo for GitHub Actions to read, but must
# never be publicly servable. Untracking these from git would stop CI from
# running at all (Actions checks the repo out and needs the workflow file
# present) — this blocks them at the edge instead, leaving both intact.
#
# The trailing "!" forces the rule even though these paths match a real
# deployed file — Cloudflare Pages serves an existing static asset before
# ever consulting _redirects, so without "!" this rule silently never
# fires. Found live on 2026-07-26: the unforced version deployed cleanly
# and both _redirects and _headers correctly 404'd on direct fetch
# (proving Cloudflare read the file), yet /.ci/check.py kept returning
# 200 — the rule existed and was never reached.
/.ci/*        /404.html   404!
/.github/*    /404.html   404!
